g"}, {"id": 1506086, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/scwa3q.jpg"}, {"id": 1506087, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/scwa3r.jpg"}, {"id": 1506088, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/scwa3s.jpg"}, {"id": 1506089, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/scwa3t.jpg"}, {"id": 1506090, "url": "//images.igdb.com/igdb/image/upload/t_thumb/scwa3u.jpg"}], "slug": "lost-altr", "summary": "LOST ALTR is a solo rogue-lite card game set within the crumbling halls of a forgotten temple. You\u2019ll face a series of Trials\u2014mysterious encounters drawn from an ever-shifting deck. Each completed Trial leads you deeper into the Ruins of ALTR. Use Aspect cards to shape your fate\u2014mysterious forces that grant you powerful advantages, but always at a cost.\n\nBuilt on the foundation of the Scoundrel card mechanics by Zach Gage and Kurt Biegand, a heavily reimagined experience, LOST ALTR blends strategy, luck, and lore in a dark, esoteric world. The path forward is never the same. The further you go, the more the ruins remember.\n\nEarly Access will evolve with new cards, mechanics, and layers of mystery\u2014shaped by feedback from those brave enough to enter the ALTR.", "themes": [{"id": 17, "name": "Fantasy"}], "url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/lost-altr"}